# BeachStar coding standards

- Apply the reviewer's CSS and values exactly as written. Say plainly if you deviate and why.
- Prefer classes with static functions. No dead code, no debug or proof hooks, no console noise. Never weaken a check to make it pass.
- Text uses px floors, `max(Npx, calc(k*var(--u)))`. Test 360x640, 500x900, 600x360, 844x390, and desktop for clipping and overlap. Non-interactive overlays get `pointer-events: none` so they don't block taps.
- Keep history linear: rebase onto origin/master, and if there are conflicts, stop for review before pushing with `--force-with-lease`. Never merge master in.
- Before reporting: run `node --check` on changed JS, load the game with the console open and confirm there are no errors, and read your full untruncated diff for stray files.
- Report only what you actually measured, and say what didn't change. Never overclaim.
- Screenshots go in the PR body as hosted artifacts, never committed.
